        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> so the text it replaces has to be the start of its filter_text (or word if it has none), otherwise it gets dropped.\r\n\r\nThanks, that clears things up. However...\r\n\r\nSince Justin asked for feedback, here's mine. I'm not the author of a completion plugin, but I'm working on completion for nvim-dap. I'm particularly concerned with a scenario that mixes the start column. The current behavior sucks, since it ends up eating the text _most of the time_, where it shouldn't:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/8710f7f7-29fc-422e-aa3e-70813f695ba4\r\n\r\nNeedless to say this is extremely annoying. I'm making a PR to no longer consume the text, but then I have the problem that for the specific item that should consume the text (the `[index]`, which should consume the `.`), it no longer does:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/97fff0c5-3f37-4d19-95f9-52fca9d81e9f\r\n\r\nHence I thought this PR would fit like a glove. Notice, however, that this replacement  **does not match the \"prefix\"**. And unlike the LSP, which I'm assuming provides detailed information about the replacement, with DAP there's much less information, e.g.:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"396\" height=\"206\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6101898f-c4a0-4f83-88a1-a18ed76f0f2b\" />\r\n\r\nWhat could be used here is the `start` _and_ some manipulation of the current line to set a `filter_text`, which feels overkill when the alternative is just allowing an _unmatching_ prefix.",
            "created_at": "2026-09-24T12:17:22Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/41938#issuecomment-5813905431",
